29:### T02 — Probability board as the opening shot (formula first, story second)
33:- **Evidence:** ev/001-bayes-board.jpg (settled board) · ev/005-board-build-mid.jpg (board mid-build, population array drawing on) · clip clips/000-bayes-board-build.mp4 (0–12 s, the layered build). Form: frame + clip (build timing).
51:- **Evidence:** ev/066-house-scene.jpg (highlight mid-line) · ev/080-house-clock-verdict.jpg (highlight at line start) · clip clips/000-bayes-board-build.mp4 (sweep visible across lines). Form: frame + clip (sweep timing is the mechanic).
57:- **Evidence:** ev/034-day1-ui-build.jpg (day 1 active, figures assembling) · ev/050-day2-resource-bars.jpg (counter over day-2 scene). Form: frame; the flip itself is a beat inside clip clips/100-chart-plunge.mp4's wider window class — ruled stills-sufficient for the counter (the claim is the state system, not the flip's easing; easing UNRESOLVED).
59:### T07 — Resource bars over standing figures (day-2 depletion scene)
63:- **Evidence:** ev/050-day2-resource-bars.jpg. Form: frame.
107:- **G-b — One notation system carries every scale (0–155 s).** Evidence: ev/001-bayes-board.jpg, ev/133-simulation-panel.jpg, ev/155-dashed-future-selves.jpg. The same icon is one person, 40 people, and 8 billion; dashed means unrealized everywhere it appears. Reason: the viewer learns the notation once and reads the whole film fluently.
113:- **B-a — The opening board is illegible at phone scale (0–13 s).** Evidence: ev/001-bayes-board.jpg — the Bayes expansion line under the formula and the callout label are small text that does not resolve at 720-wide phone playback (paraphrase-marked in T02 for exactly this reason). Timestamp-bound: the density is worst at 0–6 s, while the thesis sentence is also landing. Reason: the authority-establishing shot spends its first seconds on notation a phone viewer cannot read.
114:- **B-b — Day 2's middle beats sag (54–68 s).** Evidence: ASR 54.12–64.22 (a writer deletes his story; a lab goes dark) against census S3 (2 onsets ≥1.0 across 42.1 s) and ev/050-day2-resource-bars.jpg's held, near-empty gauges. Two catalogue beats pass with almost no visual event. Reason: the deliberate stall (G-c's price) overshoots here — the list's middle items are the likeliest drop-off window.
115:- **B-c — The day counter's state is easy to miss (32–58 s).** Evidence: ev/034-day1-ui-build.jpg, ev/050-day2-resource-bars.jpg — the counter is a small top-centre widget; at both sampled states the active cell must be looked for. Reason: the piece's only section-signalling device is its smallest element; a viewer who misses a flip loses the experiment's chronology.
138:- A Persian/English paired release study: the same episode architecture in English, testing whether the worksheet opening survives translation. (Stands on §2's consumer use + T02.)
228:### T241 — Probability board as the opening shot (formula first, story second) (P14 T02) ◆ — OWED #106
229-- Tier: **DESCRIBED — OWED #106**
230-- Mechanics: the piece opens mid-diagram, not on a title: a targeting-reticle icon at top, the star figure inside a magnifier circle, a 40-icon population array below, and the conditional-probability line P(F|H) ≈ 0.98 with its Bayes expansion typeset underneath. Elements draw on in layers over the first seconds while the voice states the thesis — the AI persona's authority is established by showing its native notation before any narrative. (Layered draw-on build — OWED: the build order is the claim, clip-cited.)
231-- Feeds: opening · diagram — P14 @ 0–13 s — ev/001-bayes-board.jpg, ev/005-board-build-mid.jpg · clips/000-bayes-board-build.mp4
- **Queue state (read this cycle):** QUEUE.md recreation section, Wave 37 update line: rows #106–#113 stand OWED from Packet #14 (T241 · T242 · T243 · T244 · T247 · T248 · T249 · T250); T241 = #106, DESCRIBED/OWED, first attempt owned by this job (A3 §3). Wave RUN.md §0b/§1 concurs. No prior scores.md, no verdict-history line, no prior attempt for T241 — FIRST ATTEMPT, no plateau to price (A2 inapplicable; stated here so Plan-exit leg 6 is answered, not skipped).
- **Consumer (named, §1.4):** the **DLC assembler opening container / diagram container** — an explainer cold-open that must establish a quantitative claim before any narrative: the board machinery (reticle + magnified subject + population array + typeset formula) is lifted whole as the opening shot of a diagram-led piece.

### 1.1 Catalogue mechanics (read firsthand)
- Digest §T02 (0–13 s): "the piece opens mid-diagram, not on a title: a targeting-reticle icon at top, the star figure inside a magnifier circle labelled (paraphrase) 'cause of failure no. 1', a 40-icon population array below, and the conditional-probability line P(F|H) ≈ 0.98 with its Bayes expansion typeset underneath. Elements draw on in layers over the first seconds while the voice states the thesis." Why: "the AI persona's authority is established by showing its native notation before any narrative."
- Style-library techniques-openings.md §T241: agrees verbatim on mechanics, window (P14 @ 0–13 s), evidence (ev/001 · ev/005 · clips/000). Tier DESCRIBED — OWED #106. No digest↔register disagreement.
- **Firsthand corrections / priced readings (binding on the build):**
  1. The board is ALREADY standing at segment t=0 (census f-0): reticle, magnifier+star+callout, full 40-icon array, formula line and expansion line 1 (partial) are all present in the first frame. The in-window motion is: expansion lines type on character-by-character (line 1 completes ≈0.8 s, line 2 ≈2.2 s, line 3 lands ≈3.4 s), corner brackets appear around the star (≈3 s), the formula's dashed condition slot fills with the condition word (≈3.5–4.0 s), the reticle pulses/dims (≈5 s), then the whole board except the array dissolves (≈5.4–6.2 s) leaving the array with the selected icon ringed. The task charge's draw-on order (reticle → magnifier+star → array → formula) is therefore built as Act 1's compressed allocation — named as a departure in §2.2, not hidden.
  2. The array is 4 rows × 10 = 40 icons (counted firsthand, ev/001 + census f-0); every small icon carries a small plus/star chest glyph; the selected icon (row 1, index 5, 0-based col 5) is circled and is the magnifier's source (two diagonal connector lines run from the magnifier circle down to it).
  3. The expansion is THREE typeset lines under the formula (ev/005 + census f-3/f-4), not one: line 1 the Bayes ratio with values, line 2 a summation/Poisson line, line 3 the result line "⇒ P(F|H) = 0.9811 ± 0.004 (p < 0.001)". ev/001 shows only line 1 because it is an earlier settled frame.
  4. The creator's burned-in karaoke captions along the bottom are a specimen property, NOT part of this technique — excluded from the build (fleet no-captions law; §6.5). The Persian callout/formula words are technique text (subject), rendered from CONFIG strings in Latin transliteration of the same notation (P(F|H) form) — the build's default texts are the notation lines themselves, which are language-neutral; the callout default is the English gloss "cause of failure no. 1" / "failure" (digest's own gloss), priced here as a reading, not smuggled as specimen text.

